<section class="section" style="padding-top:65px"><div class="container docs-layout"><aside class="docs-sidebar"><span class="eyebrow">Docs</span><h4>AI</h4><a href="#overview">Overview</a><a href="#agents">AI Agents</a><a href="#knowledge">Knowledge</a><a href="#workflows">Workflows</a><a href="#handoff">Human Handoff</a><a href="#voice">Voice AI</a><h4>Related</h4><a href="/channels.php">Lead Channels</a><a href="/crm.php">CRM</a><a href="/api/">API</a></aside><article class="doc-article"><span class="eyebrow">AI platform guide</span><h1>AI Agents in Ally</h1><p class="hero-copy" style="margin:0">Use AI as an operational layer across lead capture, conversations, qualification, follow-up, appointments, sales and support.</p><div id="overview" class="callout"><strong>Core idea:</strong> AI agents work with CRM context. Their conversations and actions should update the same lead record your human team uses.</div><h2 id="agents">AI Agents</h2><p>Ally supports specialized agent roles such as Lead Capture, Lead Qualification, WhatsApp, Voice, Follow-up, Appointment Booking, Nurturing, Sales Assistant, Support, Reactivation and Campaign agents. Each agent can have its own objective, instructions, knowledge, limits and escalation behavior.</p><h3>Agent configuration</h3><ul><li>Model and model-specific settings</li><li>System prompt and role instructions</li><li>Approved knowledge sources</li><li>Response and usage controls</li><li>Business-hour and escalation rules</li><li>Human handoff destinations</li><li>Activity and outcome logging</li></ul><h2 id="knowledge">Knowledge grounding</h2><p>Agents should use approved business knowledge when answering questions. Maintain knowledge sources as products, policies, pricing, services and customer questions evolve. Review unanswered or uncertain questions to identify knowledge gaps.</p><h2 id="workflows">Agentic workflows</h2><p>Agents can be connected through automation. A typical lead workflow can create or match a lead, start a conversation, collect qualification data, score intent, schedule a follow-up or appointment, and route high-intent prospects to a human.</p><div class="code">New Lead
  → Lead Capture Agent
  → Qualification Agent
  → Lead Score / Intent
  → Follow-up or Appointment Agent
  → Human Handoff when required
  → CRM / Pipeline update</div><h2 id="handoff">Human handoff</h2><p>Define clear conditions for escalation. Examples include high-value leads, negotiation requests, sensitive cases, unsupported questions or explicit requests to speak with a person. The handoff should include the AI summary, qualification answers, intent, history and recommended next action.</p><h2 id="voice">Voice AI</h2><p>Voice agents can support inbound and outbound calling, lead qualification, appointment booking, call summaries, analysis and authorized human transfers. Phone numbers, provider configuration and call policies should be managed by administrators.</p><div class="callout">Production AI models, provider credentials and channel credentials should be configured in the authenticated Ally environment. Do not place API secrets in public website code.</div></article></div></section><?php include __DIR__.'/../includes/footer.php'; ?>